  "caption": "Quinn's first step every morning felt like stepping on a Lego brick. Months of stretching and foot rolling later, the heel was still grumpy.\n\nPlantar heel pain often behaves like a load problem, and adding high-load calf strengthening can help recovery in the first few months.\n\nWhat can help: single-leg heel raises with a rolled towel under the toes, done slowly (3 seconds up, 2 hold, 3 down), every second day. Start with 3 sets of 12 and drop toward 8 reps as you add load with a backpack — and keep stretching too.\n\nGet it checked if heel pain followed a fall or knock, or comes with swelling, numbness or tingling, severe night pain, or feeling unwell.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
